<article class="env-definition" id="05K9">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/05K9">Definition <span data-tag="05K9">10.28.2</span>.</a> Let $R$ be a ring. Let $\mathcal{F}$ be a set of ideals of $R$. We say $\mathcal{F}$ is an <em>Oka family</em> if $R \in \mathcal{F}$ and whenever $I \subset R$ is an ideal and $(I : a), (I, a) \in \mathcal{F}$ for some $a \in R$, then $I \in \mathcal{F}$. </p>
